.TH GIT-@-SPROUT 1 "August 2025" "GitAT v1.1.0" "Git Workflow Management Tool"
.SH NAME
git-@-sprout \- Manage working branch configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git @ sprout
[\fIACTION\fR] [\fIBRANCH-NAME\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBsprout\fR command manages Git branches with interactive creation, deletion, and switching. It was renamed from the original \fBbranch\fR command to avoid conflicts with standard Git commands.
.PP
The command provides a comprehensive interface for branch management with interactive prompts and validation.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B list
List all branches (default action)
.TP
.B create
Create a new branch
.TP
.B delete
Delete a branch
.TP
.B switch
Switch to a different branch
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B BRANCH-NAME
Name of the branch to operate on (required for create, delete, and switch actions)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
List all branches:
.RS
.nf
git @ sprout
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a new branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ sprout create new-feature
.fi
.RE
.PP
Delete a branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ sprout delete old-feature
.fi
.RE
.PP
Switch to a branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ sprout switch develop
.fi
.RE
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
.PP
If no arguments are provided, the command will show an interactive form to select the action and branch.
.SH VALIDATION
.PP
The command performs several validation checks:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Ensures we're in a Git repository
.IP \(bu 2
Validates branch names
.IP \(bu 2
Prevents deletion of protected branches (master, main, develop, trunk)
.IP \(bu 2
Confirms destructive operations
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
.BR git-@ (1),
.BR git-@-work (1),
.BR git-@-sweep (1)